1
00:00:06,780 --> 00:00:12,060
=Fatal Proximity to Him=

2
00:00:12,060 --> 00:00:14,100
=Episode 21=

3
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:21,020
Xiyu.

4
00:00:22,660 --> 00:00:23,260
Xiyu?

5
00:00:27,780 --> 00:00:28,420
Xiyu!

6
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:29,620
Xiyu!

7
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:31,660
No.

8
00:00:32,220 --> 00:00:32,580
No.

9
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:34,220
No!

10
00:00:42,020 --> 00:00:42,780
(He Lan,)

11
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:44,620
(you can't change fate.)

12
00:00:44,940 --> 00:00:46,260
(Stop trying.)

13
00:00:50,060 --> 00:00:51,900
Why won't you just leave us alone?

14
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:54,820
Give Xiyu back to me!

15
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:57,660
(Give up.)

16
00:01:00,180 --> 00:01:01,500
You want me to give up?

17
00:01:03,420 --> 00:01:04,620
Never!

18
00:01:34,700 --> 00:01:35,740
Why?

19
00:01:36,380 --> 00:01:37,300
How is this possible?

20
00:01:47,380 --> 00:01:48,260
I died again.

21
00:01:48,460 --> 00:01:49,380
How did I die?

22
00:01:49,900 --> 00:01:51,460
I only remember blowing out the candles.

23
00:01:52,980 --> 00:01:53,660
It's okay.

24
00:01:54,580 --> 00:01:55,620
We'll try again.

25
00:01:58,220 --> 00:01:59,260
What did you do?

26
00:02:00,548 --> 00:02:04,420
♪I hide my racing heart without a sound♪

27
00:02:04,420 --> 00:02:05,060
Does it hurt?

28
00:02:07,377 --> 00:02:12,017
♪I close my eyes and pretend
the story's been reset♪

29
00:02:13,451 --> 00:02:16,177
♪I steer clear of every path
that leads to you♪

30
00:02:16,480 --> 00:02:19,497
♪Trying to outrun the storm
we're destined for♪

31
00:02:19,982 --> 00:02:22,205
♪I thought if I didn't hear, see,
or speak of you♪

32
00:02:22,210 --> 00:02:25,577
♪I could cut every thread
that ties us together♪

33
00:02:30,380 --> 00:02:31,940
There's one thing
I still don't understand.

34
00:02:33,100 --> 00:02:35,100
Based on how things originally happened,

35
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:37,500
we didn't know Li Junsheng
was making fake drugs.

36
00:02:37,860 --> 00:02:39,460
We didn't know about
Zhang Jichuan either,

37
00:02:39,780 --> 00:02:41,580
let alone reported Li Junsheng
and had him sent to prison.

38
00:02:42,020 --> 00:02:44,140
So why does Zhang Jinghang
hate us so much?

39
00:02:44,140 --> 00:02:45,540
Why does he want me dead?

40
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:46,820
I was wondering that too.

41
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:48,900
When I found out Zhang Jinghang's dad

42
00:02:48,900 --> 00:02:50,020
was Zhang Jichuan,

43
00:02:50,460 --> 00:02:51,500
I suddenly remembered something.

44
00:02:52,020 --> 00:02:54,540
During a power struggle
at Yunshan Group,

45
00:02:54,900 --> 00:02:56,140
I cut several business lines.

46
00:02:56,700 --> 00:02:57,900
One of the suppliers

47
00:02:58,260 --> 00:02:59,660
was Zhang Jichuan's company.

48
00:03:00,860 --> 00:03:02,140
His company later went bankrupt.

49
00:03:02,940 --> 00:03:04,020
So that's what happened.

50
00:03:07,220 --> 00:03:07,940
I get it now.

51
00:03:10,260 --> 00:03:10,940
I get it.

52
00:03:11,060 --> 00:03:12,900
Previously, we learned that
Zhang Jinghang was arrested,

53
00:03:13,060 --> 00:03:14,420
but he was still full of resentment.

54
00:03:14,460 --> 00:03:15,060
So...

55
00:03:17,740 --> 00:03:19,900
We have to help him
let go of that resentment.

56
00:03:20,540 --> 00:03:22,380
That's the only way to truly
change the ending.

57
00:03:23,380 --> 00:03:24,140
Don't panic.

58
00:03:24,540 --> 00:03:25,700
We'll figure it out together.

59
00:03:26,180 --> 00:03:27,340
No matter how many times
we went through the loop,

60
00:03:27,340 --> 00:03:28,380
I was never afraid.

61
00:03:29,540 --> 00:03:30,500
Because I believed

62
00:03:31,420 --> 00:03:32,660
that if we found the real killer,

63
00:03:32,660 --> 00:03:33,620
I could save you.

64
00:03:34,740 --> 00:03:35,780
But now...

65
00:03:54,260 --> 00:03:55,980
We can't ignore the fake drugs.

66
00:03:57,700 --> 00:03:59,620
I want to see if we can help
Zhang Jinghang.

67
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:02,820
He's only seventeen.

68
00:04:03,300 --> 00:04:04,780
He still has his whole life
ahead of him.

69
00:04:07,380 --> 00:04:07,860
Okay.

70
00:04:12,220 --> 00:04:12,780
What's wrong,

71
00:04:12,940 --> 00:04:13,540
Xiyu?

72
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:15,340
I want to take you somewhere.

73
00:04:24,020 --> 00:04:25,540
She has hepatitis C too.

74
00:04:26,780 --> 00:04:28,020
She's only two years younger than us.

75
00:04:28,860 --> 00:04:31,180
But she took medicine
with poor quality control

76
00:04:31,900 --> 00:04:33,060
and developed acute kidney failure.

77
00:04:33,460 --> 00:04:35,260
Now she needs dialysis to stay alive.

78
00:04:36,260 --> 00:04:37,540
At least she's still alive.

79
00:04:38,340 --> 00:04:39,820
There was also a forty-year-old man.

80
00:04:40,860 --> 00:04:41,900
He passed away.

81
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:44,100
His son is only ten.

82
00:04:45,380 --> 00:04:46,700
Why are you telling me all this?

83
00:04:47,540 --> 00:04:48,300
Zhang Jinghang,

84
00:04:49,660 --> 00:04:51,180
we know what your dad is doing.

85
00:04:51,780 --> 00:04:53,820
His fake drug operation has to stop.

86
00:04:54,180 --> 00:04:56,100
Otherwise, more and more people
will get hurt.

87
00:05:00,860 --> 00:05:02,540
Since you already know,

88
00:05:03,580 --> 00:05:04,660
then you should be aware

89
00:05:05,220 --> 00:05:07,340
that the effective cure for this disease
is way too expensive.

90
00:05:08,500 --> 00:05:10,540
My dad only started making the medicine
to treat my mom.

91
00:05:11,100 --> 00:05:13,100
People from her patient group
came begging him for it.

92
00:05:13,420 --> 00:05:14,820
That's why he gave it to them.

93
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:16,940
Most people who buy it

94
00:05:17,900 --> 00:05:20,300
have advanced hepatitis C.

95
00:05:21,140 --> 00:05:22,780
They need it to stay alive.

96
00:05:24,460 --> 00:05:25,020
Besides,

97
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:26,620
developing a drug requires funding.

98
00:05:27,140 --> 00:05:29,020
My dad charges only a third
of the brand-name price.

99
00:05:29,540 --> 00:05:30,420
My mom takes it too.

100
00:05:30,940 --> 00:05:32,220
She's never had any problems.

101
00:05:33,860 --> 00:05:35,380
Are you sure the medicine your mom takes

102
00:05:35,380 --> 00:05:36,580
is the same stuff they get?

103
00:05:37,660 --> 00:05:39,020
He may not listen to anyone else,

104
00:05:39,540 --> 00:05:40,740
but you're his son.

105
00:05:40,900 --> 00:05:42,060
Tell him that he has to stop.

106
00:05:49,460 --> 00:05:50,620
If he doesn't stop,

107
00:05:51,460 --> 00:05:52,580
we'll report him.

108
00:06:09,820 --> 00:06:10,940
(Medical Ice Pack)

109
00:06:10,940 --> 00:06:11,420
I don't need it.

110
00:06:11,980 --> 00:06:12,580
It's just a scratch.

111
00:06:15,860 --> 00:06:17,060
Those people have no conscience.

112
00:06:17,700 --> 00:06:18,540
Something goes wrong after they take it,

113
00:06:19,060 --> 00:06:20,380
and they come here making a scene.

114
00:06:21,020 --> 00:06:22,140
If they want something safe
and reliable,

115
00:06:22,380 --> 00:06:23,220
they can pay up

116
00:06:23,260 --> 00:06:24,100
and buy the brand-name drug.

117
00:06:24,380 --> 00:06:26,540
You think making medicine in secret
is easy?

118
00:06:27,420 --> 00:06:28,220
You think it takes no time?

119
00:06:28,700 --> 00:06:29,860
No money?

120
00:06:31,460 --> 00:06:31,900
Dad,

121
00:06:33,380 --> 00:06:34,180
that medicine...

122
00:06:35,020 --> 00:06:36,180
maybe you should stop making it.

123
00:06:37,180 --> 00:06:38,780
Business has been bad
these past two years.

124
00:06:40,420 --> 00:06:41,540
If I stop selling the medicine,

125
00:06:42,860 --> 00:06:44,540
how will I afford the brand-name drug
for your mom?

126
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:47,420
Mom's been taking the brand-name drug
all along?

127
00:06:48,140 --> 00:06:49,020
Of course.

128
00:06:50,060 --> 00:06:51,740
I'd never risk your mom's life.

129
00:06:52,580 --> 00:06:53,660
Most of the medicine I make

130
00:06:54,140 --> 00:06:55,380
is perfectly fine.

131
00:06:56,260 --> 00:06:57,060
But after all,

132
00:06:57,420 --> 00:06:58,380
it's a small operation.

133
00:06:59,180 --> 00:07:00,780
I can't guarantee quality
every single time.

134
00:07:01,620 --> 00:07:03,100
But they know

135
00:07:03,620 --> 00:07:05,220
buying fake drugs is illegal.

136
00:07:05,580 --> 00:07:06,580
(Medical Ice Pack)
So if something goes wrong,

137
00:07:07,500 --> 00:07:08,340
they won't dare make
a big deal out of it.

138
00:07:09,580 --> 00:07:10,420
Don't ever

139
00:07:11,060 --> 00:07:12,580
let your mom find out these things.

140
00:07:13,340 --> 00:07:14,060
But Dad...

141
00:07:14,420 --> 00:07:15,380
I'm afraid one day...

142
00:07:15,700 --> 00:07:16,420
Don't worry.

143
00:07:16,780 --> 00:07:17,700
None of this

144
00:07:17,820 --> 00:07:18,700
is your concern.

145
00:07:19,060 --> 00:07:19,860
All you need to do

146
00:07:19,900 --> 00:07:21,180
is focus on your studies

147
00:07:21,220 --> 00:07:22,340
and prepare for
the college entrance exam.

148
00:07:23,140 --> 00:07:24,100
You and your mom

149
00:07:24,100 --> 00:07:25,820
are the most important people
in my life.

150
00:07:27,500 --> 00:07:28,420
For the two of you,

151
00:07:29,220 --> 00:07:30,420
I'd do anything.

152
00:07:32,860 --> 00:07:33,980
Everyone has their own suffering.

153
00:07:35,420 --> 00:07:36,940
Every family has its own fate.

154
00:07:37,780 --> 00:07:39,100
The only people I can protect

155
00:07:42,460 --> 00:07:44,060
are my own family.

156
00:07:50,100 --> 00:07:53,340
(Medical Ice Pack)

157
00:07:55,900 --> 00:07:56,420
Dad,

158
00:07:57,260 --> 00:07:58,340
you should run.

159
00:08:00,380 --> 00:08:01,260
I knew it.

160
00:08:02,340 --> 00:08:03,700
Getting someone to listen to
their conscience

161
00:08:04,500 --> 00:08:05,620
isn't that easy.

162
00:08:11,500 --> 00:08:12,820
I went to the police yesterday
to report him.

163
00:08:13,260 --> 00:08:14,540
I heard Zhang Jichuan was arrested.

164
00:08:15,380 --> 00:08:16,580
Zhang Jinghang turned him in.

165
00:08:18,140 --> 00:08:19,820
But I still can't figure out

166
00:08:20,220 --> 00:08:21,100
what made Zhang Jinghang

167
00:08:21,180 --> 00:08:22,900
suddenly grow a conscience.

168
00:08:42,140 --> 00:08:42,820
Ma'am.

169
00:08:50,100 --> 00:08:51,300
Xiyu?

170
00:08:51,340 --> 00:08:51,940
Easy.

171
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:54,820
What brings you here?

172
00:08:56,540 --> 00:08:58,740
I know it's not visiting hours,

173
00:08:59,220 --> 00:09:00,540
but I couldn't wait any longer.

174
00:09:01,020 --> 00:09:02,580
I have to talk to you.

175
00:09:03,700 --> 00:09:04,780
What's wrong, sweetheart?

176
00:09:07,060 --> 00:09:08,740
You love Zhang Jinghang
very much, right?

177
00:09:10,100 --> 00:09:10,780
Of course.

178
00:09:11,220 --> 00:09:13,020
What mother doesn't love her child?

179
00:09:14,060 --> 00:09:15,900
Zhang Jinghang has always
gotten good grades.

180
00:09:16,380 --> 00:09:18,100
I'm sure he'll get into medical school

181
00:09:18,380 --> 00:09:19,540
and become a doctor.

182
00:09:21,380 --> 00:09:21,980
Yes.

183
00:09:23,860 --> 00:09:25,140
Because I've always been in poor health,

184
00:09:26,380 --> 00:09:27,460
he listed medicine

185
00:09:27,660 --> 00:09:28,140
as his

186
00:09:28,180 --> 00:09:28,900
major preference.

187
00:09:29,260 --> 00:09:30,060
And he's really

188
00:09:30,060 --> 00:09:30,860
made me proud.

189
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:33,500
But...

190
00:09:34,300 --> 00:09:35,900
what his father is doing now

191
00:09:36,140 --> 00:09:37,060
could ruin his life.

192
00:09:38,420 --> 00:09:40,500
Do you know his father
is making generic drugs?

193
00:09:41,220 --> 00:09:41,940
What?

194
00:09:41,980 --> 00:09:43,220
What generic drugs?

195
00:09:43,500 --> 00:09:45,580
When his father went abroad
to buy medicine for you,

196
00:09:45,860 --> 00:09:47,780
he got the idea to make his own
generic version.

197
00:09:48,060 --> 00:09:49,500
He's been making it in secret
for a long time.

198
00:09:50,020 --> 00:09:51,420
People have already died from it.

199
00:09:52,180 --> 00:09:54,300
Jinghang is helping his dad
flee the country.

200
00:09:55,380 --> 00:09:56,460
Jinghang would never do that.

201
00:09:56,740 --> 00:09:57,340
Ma'am,

202
00:09:57,620 --> 00:09:58,700
if he turns himself in now,

203
00:09:58,700 --> 00:10:00,300
there's still a chance
for a lighter sentence.

204
00:10:00,340 --> 00:10:01,820
But once he flees the country,

205
00:10:01,860 --> 00:10:02,940
that's a whole different matter.

206
00:10:03,140 --> 00:10:04,380
Jinghang could also

207
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:05,700
be charged with helping
his father evade arrest.

208
00:10:06,220 --> 00:10:06,700
Then

209
00:10:06,700 --> 00:10:08,780
his father will spend his life
in hiding,

210
00:10:08,980 --> 00:10:10,020
and Jinghang will be tied down
because of this

211
00:10:10,020 --> 00:10:11,780
for the rest of his life.

212
00:10:12,140 --> 00:10:12,780
No.

213
00:10:13,460 --> 00:10:14,100
It can't be.

214
00:10:15,860 --> 00:10:16,220
No.

215
00:10:16,220 --> 00:10:16,740
Ma'am,

216
00:10:18,060 --> 00:10:19,540
I believe you're the only one

217
00:10:19,540 --> 00:10:20,740
who can get through
to Zhang Jinghang now.

218
00:10:21,660 --> 00:10:22,580
You love him so much.

219
00:10:22,980 --> 00:10:24,940
Please stop him before it's too late.

220
00:10:25,260 --> 00:10:26,300
Make him walk away from this.

221
00:10:33,900 --> 00:10:36,260
I never thought the one person
who could get through to Zhang Jinghang

222
00:10:36,740 --> 00:10:37,660
would be his mother.

223
00:10:37,820 --> 00:10:38,260
Yeah.

224
00:10:39,260 --> 00:10:41,260
A mother's love for her child

225
00:10:41,460 --> 00:10:42,940
is stronger than her love
for her own life.

226
00:10:43,540 --> 00:10:44,180
And besides,

227
00:10:44,180 --> 00:10:45,620
Zhang Jinghang really cares
about his mother.

228
00:10:46,060 --> 00:10:46,860
I don't know

229
00:10:46,860 --> 00:10:48,300
what she said to him,

230
00:10:48,580 --> 00:10:49,060
but...

231
00:10:49,420 --> 00:10:50,140
clearly,

232
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:52,140
she changed the course
of Zhang Jinghang's life

233
00:10:53,180 --> 00:10:54,420
and saved his future.

234
00:10:55,700 --> 00:10:56,300
From now on,

235
00:10:56,300 --> 00:10:57,740
if Zhang Jinghang ever needs help,

236
00:10:57,940 --> 00:10:59,300
let's do whatever we can

237
00:10:59,420 --> 00:11:00,540
to help him out.

238
00:11:00,900 --> 00:11:01,380
Okay.

239
00:11:05,420 --> 00:11:07,260
I don't know what our lives
will look like

240
00:11:07,260 --> 00:11:08,420
ten years from now.

241
00:11:09,340 --> 00:11:10,380
We've done everything we can.

242
00:11:10,980 --> 00:11:11,820
I'm tired too.

243
00:11:12,540 --> 00:11:13,780
From now on,

244
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:15,980
I just want to enjoy life

245
00:11:16,180 --> 00:11:17,340
and do something meaningful.

246
00:11:18,540 --> 00:11:19,340
Will you do that with me?

247
00:11:21,700 --> 00:11:22,260
Of course.

248
00:11:50,230 --> 00:11:55,520
♪I hide my racing heart without a sound♪

249
00:11:56,930 --> 00:12:01,730
♪I close my eyes and pretend
the story's been reset♪

250
00:12:03,060 --> 00:12:06,080
♪I steer clear of every path
that leads to you♪

251
00:12:06,080 --> 00:12:09,070
♪Trying to outrun the storm
we're destined for♪

252
00:12:09,590 --> 00:12:11,790
♪I thought if I didn't hear, see,
or speak of you♪

253
00:12:11,790 --> 00:12:15,240
♪I could cut every thread
that ties us together♪

254
00:12:16,470 --> 00:12:21,490
♪Through the endless night,
I guard my only secret♪

255
00:12:23,070 --> 00:12:28,090
♪In this new cycle, I watch you
become innocent again♪

256
00:12:29,250 --> 00:12:31,380
♪I tried to erase the fire we once had♪

257
00:12:31,380 --> 00:12:35,130
♪But I can't erase your name
carved into my bones♪

258
00:12:35,890 --> 00:12:38,070
♪The more I try to leave you behind♪

259
00:12:38,070 --> 00:12:42,330
♪The deeper I sink with no end in sight♪

260
00:12:42,330 --> 00:12:44,860
♪What if I stayed a little farther away♪

261
00:12:44,860 --> 00:12:48,530
♪Could I finally break free
from this cycle♪

262
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:50,880
♪What if I took things a little slower♪

263
00:12:50,880 --> 00:12:55,110
♪Could I delay the moment
everything falls apart♪

264
00:12:55,110 --> 00:12:58,910
♪Maybe if I retreat to the edge
of my dreams♪

265
00:12:58,910 --> 00:13:01,920
♪I could give you another future♪

266
00:13:02,240 --> 00:13:08,470
♪A tomorrow where I no longer exist♪

267
00:13:08,470 --> 00:13:10,740
♪Even if I never want to see you again♪

268
00:13:10,740 --> 00:13:12,380
♪This nightmare still won't end♪

269
00:13:12,380 --> 00:13:14,240
♪Even if it all plays out again♪

270
00:13:14,240 --> 00:13:16,430
♪I'll still find my way back to you♪

271
00:13:16,430 --> 00:13:20,330
♪Even if having you only leaves me
in your debt♪

272
00:13:20,330 --> 00:13:24,320
♪It's still better than
losing you forever♪
